Retry-policy harness added to `tests/unit/test-post-release-dev-sync.mjs` — 14 `{ todo: true }` tests (the node:test red-first analogue of `pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True)`, mirroring SA-0MW3GCHEL001G8CP), all driven through the existing `options.run` seam plus an injected `options.sleep` so no test sleeps and no real repository is touched:

- transport-class allowlist retried then succeeds (connection closed by remote host, connection reset, `RPC failed`, early EOF, TLS/SSL, proxy, timeout);
- an unrecognised failure fails closed (allowlist, never replayed — `git merge` is not idempotent);
- 3 attempts / 500 ms doubling by default, with `attempts`/`backoffMs`/`sleep` overrides;
- deterministic failures (merge conflict, `[rejected]` non-fast-forward, missing remote ref) produce exactly one attempt, no sleep, `{ success: false }`;
- every retry replays fetch → checkout → merge → push, never just the failed command.

Contract pinned for the implementation item SA-0MWXMTQ4Q001N0WJ: result records `result.attempts`. Node suite run via the test skill: 900 tests, 0 failures, 16 todo (2 pre-existing + 14 new). Markers are removed by SA-0MWXMTQ4Q001N0WJ.
